Z||000000||Scott||05-22-2001||12:23 AM||||Hi Folks,<BR>  I'm new here, and I really like this site.  Anyway... here's my problem: I don't have dash lights on my '85 Duke SE.  I had to park it almost 2 years ago, and last weekend when I checked it out I couldn't get the dash lights to work.  I took the dash apart, but couldn't find anything that looked out of the ordinary.  The fuses are good too.  I believe that I once saw a thread about this problem in a FOCOA mag, which described a rheostat, heat sink, or somethingy that is located under the steering column that can cause this.  Does anybody know how to fix such a problem?<BR>The electrically ungifted,<BR>Scott||||reg||5
Z||000001||mbramble||05-22-2001||09:03 AM||||Is it just the instrument panel lights??  How about other lights such as the light in the A/C contol panel, the radio, lighted trunk release and/or defogger switch, and the shift indicator light (for auto).  Do any of these other lights come on and dim/brighten with the dimmer control under the headlight switch?? ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Scott||05-22-2001||10:51 AM||||Just the dash is unlit for sure.  It wasn't dark enough to discern if the heater/AC controls (& etc.) weren't working.  The radio was lit though, and seemed to dim just fine; so I don't think the dimmer rheostat is the problem. ||||reg||10
